{"id":3515,"date":"2017-03-18T06:38:55","date_gmt":"2017-03-18T13:38:55","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=3515"},"modified":"2017-03-18T06:38:55","modified_gmt":"2017-03-18T13:38:55","slug":"a-little-gem-in-central-texas","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2017\/03\/18\/a-little-gem-in-central-texas\/","title":{"rendered":"A Little Gem in Central Texas"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>We left the <a href=\"http:\/\/www.skpranch.com\/\" target=\"_blank\">SKP park<\/a> at Lakewood, NM Thursday morning and the map told us that State Route 285 would be a direct route down through Carlsbad and on to I-10 where we&#8217;d head east.<\/p>\n<p>Yes, it was &#8220;direct&#8221; but FILLED with all kinds of tanker trucks and heavy equipment working the oil fields that lined the state route on both sides of the highway. \u00a0As far as the eye could see, it was nothing but gas and oil wells and all the trucks and equipment to service those rigs. (Ugh)<a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright size-medium wp-image-3526\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30-300x169.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-09.50.30.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a><\/p>\n<p>Additionally, the asphalt was pretty bumpy having been heaved over and over by the heavy trucks day after day. \u00a0Although the speed limit was 75 mph (and the trucks liked to do it), I wouldn&#8217;t subject the coach (pulling the car) and the two of us to the high speeds with all the bumping and rolling this way and that.<\/p>\n<p>All in all, it was a LONG drive down to I-10 to Pecos, TX (100+ miles) where we were FINALLY able to get on SMOOTH I-10 and head east.<\/p>\n<p>We then drove about 4 hours east to a great little RV park we found on <a href=\"http:\/\/www.allstays.com\" target=\"_blank\">Allstays.com<\/a>. \u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.rvparkreviews.com\/regions\/texas\/junction\/pecan-valley-rv-park\" target=\"_blank\">Pecan Valley RV Park<\/a> boasts only 14 sites, (3 are full-timers and 2 are tent sites), but our host David told us on the phone he had a great 60&#8242; 50amp pull-thru site that would be great for us.<\/p>\n<p>The park is nestled a few thousand feet off the road behind a HUGE pecan grove and up against the North Llamo River.<\/p>\n<p>Although there was no Verizon coverage and no television, we&#8217;d definately stop here again. \u00a0David was a gracious host, the park was spotless (see the slide show below) and the setting was peaceful and relaxing. \u00a0We cooked brats on the grill, sat out a bit and when we slept, it was with the windows open all night. \u00a0And NO traffic noise.<\/p>\n<p>Beautiful and peaceful. \u00a0Pictures below.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-3515 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-large'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.41.43.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.07.12.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"685\" height=\"385\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59-1024x576.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2017\/03\/2017-03-16-18.02.59.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 685px) 100vw, 685px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a h